                                h2.fw-normal.text-primary.mb-4 Sports 
                                p.fw-normal.text-secondary Qatar’s sports investments have transformed the country’s global reputation and positioned the country as a key player in the international sports business landscape, aligned with the goals outlined in the Qatar National Vision 2030.<br><br> Following the success of global events such as the FIFA World Cup 2022™, Qatar has continued to expand its $20 billion+ sports economy. The nation now hosts over 80 international sporting events annually, including landmark occasions like the Formula 1 Qatar Grand Prix 2025, the 2030 Asian Games and a bid to host the 2036 Olympics and Paralympic Games.<br><br>Each event attracts a wealth of allied sub-sectors and industries, from facilities management to sports education, sports medicine, tourism, data and analytics, and merchandising, turning billions in profit and underpinning Qatar’s position as an attractive business destination for global sports companies.<br><br>The Qatar Financial Centre (QFC) plays a central role in enabling this growth. Through initiatives like the QFC Sports Accelerator, developed in collaboration with the Aspire Zone Foundation and its partnership with Qatar Development Bank (QDB) to support Qatar SportsTech, QFC provides a platform for both local and international sports-focused startups and enterprises.<br><br>QFC provides direct access to Qatar's sports economy, a rapidly growing industry brimming with innovation, commercial opportunity, and regional reach, for foreign businesses wishing to enter the MENA market.<br><br>QFC provides direct access for international firms wanting to enter Qatar’s rapidly expanding sports sector and gain access to the wider region.

                .slide-item
