                                h2.fw-normal.text-primary.mb-4 Digital & Media 
                                p.fw-normal.text-secondary Qatar’s fast-growing digital and media sector continues to unlock new opportunities for collaboration across ministries, government agencies and private enterprises. As a regional leader in digital adoption, the country is attracting global interest from companies looking to explore its connected and innovation-driven market.<br><br> As Qatar pushes forward with its ambitious development goals, it aims to generate QAR 40 billion in digital sector GDP impact by 2030 and create 26,000 new jobs, strengthening its role as a global leader in the digital economy.
                                p.fw-normal.text-secondary Key areas driving this momentum include: 
                                ul 
                                    
                                    li.fw-normal.text-secondary Cloud computing
                                    li.fw-normal.text-secondary Cybersecurity
                                    li.fw-normal.text-secondary Artificial Intelligence (AI)
                                    li.fw-normal.text-secondary Blockchain
                                    li.fw-normal.text-secondary Internet of Things (IoT)
                                    li.fw-normal.text-secondary AR/VR, e-commerce, and data analytics
                                p.fw-normal.text-secondary QFC offers competitive benefits and incentives to digital service firms looking to set up businesses or expand their operations in Qatar, including initiatives such as the QFC Tech Circle, a shared working space for eligible tech firms and the knowledge-exchange platform QFC Tech Talk Series.
